h1 -- kbd privacy policy

p -- Effective October 14, 2026

p --
  Nothing you type leaves your device. kbd has no accounts, no analytics and no
  tracking, and the keyboard has no network access and does not use Full Access.

p --
  To work, kbd stores a few small files on your iPhone, inside the keyboard's
  own storage: words you add, email addresses you choose to remember, your emoji
  history, and numbers describing where your thumb lands on the keys. They never
  leave your phone, and deleting the app deletes them. kbd also reads your Text
  Replacements and contact names from iOS to offer as suggestions, and keeps
  them only in memory.

h2 -- Train swipes

p
  --
  What you donate from the app's Train swipes screen is your swipes on its
  sentences, the finger and setting you pick, your phone's model and screen
  size, and the app's version, under a random ID. This site keeps when each
  arrived; your IP address only limits how often it accepts requests, and isn't
  stored. At the first monthly release 30 days after it arrives, what you sent
  joins the public dataset, free for anyone to use (CC0), at${" "}
  --
  a href="/app/kbd/training" -- lavalva.dev/app/kbd/training
  --
  , with a hash of the ID, which groups your sets, in place of the ID. Delete it
  there any time with the ID: it leaves this site at once and the dataset at its
  next release, except copies already downloaded.
  --

p -- Questions: kbd@lavalva.dev
